{"id":"lm-68151bf7e755f1777c2c01e4","title":"A Learnable Austria - RegionGHGuessing","group":"LM Europe","desc":"learnablemeta.com map","cards":[{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/cvJf1NJtcH0RrOlgDJ7VAGNbkviShbprE17e.avif"],"a":"Alps","slug":"austria","note":"<p>The <strong>highest parts</strong> of the <strong>Alps</strong> are in <strong>western</strong> and <strong>central Switzerland</strong>. The tallest peaks are on the Italian border in Austria’s panhandle, known for their <strong>sharp</strong>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/@47.1389084,10.2855156,3a,75y,66.33h,92.53t/data=!3m8!1e1!3m6!1sTDJ_tFCAlBIH4nUIgmkiMw!2e0!5s20200901T000000!6shttps:%2F%2Fstreetviewpixels-pa.googleapis.com%2Fv1%2Fthumbnail%3Fcb_client%3Dmaps_sv.tactile%26w%3D900%26h%3D600%26pitch%3D-2.530000000000001%26panoid%3DTDJ_tFCAlBIH4nUIgmkiMw%26yaw%3D66.33!7i16384!8i8192?entry=ttu&#x26;g_ep=EgoyMDI1MDQyOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>dramatic appearance</strong></a>.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/nhL8KMC9M5w4oYiU4I51jyWhQur0bmGqVJr8.avif"],"a":"Burgenland Güterweg Sign","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Green</strong> “<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%BCterweg\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Güterweg</strong></a>” signs are found in <strong>Burgenland</strong>.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/ziriLgrHQk0wW1gJycJ9UyhWV2apeRLybQlQ.avif"],"a":"Dornbirn Street Signs","slug":"austria","note":"<p>In <strong>Dornbirn</strong> you can find <strong>red streetsigns</strong></p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/L5GMvSE15KNqjRx4FxjaRXe4bwx7seWv3DJb.avif"],"a":"Graz Bus","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Graz</strong>´s public transport company is called \"<strong>Graz Holding</strong>\". The logo of it can be seen on busses/trams in this region.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/cWEaB66HzXQnDi4wRf2bi8O4Exoso93QgXzR.avif"],"a":"Graz Street Signs","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>In Graz</strong> you can find <strong>green streetsigns</strong> with <strong>2 lines</strong>.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/foDhys04vRI7iJ1I3UNQAmJQFZF6OOH34uiR.avif"],"a":"Innsbruck Street Sign","slug":"austria","note":"<p>In <strong>Innsbruck</strong> you can find <strong>large streetsigns</strong> with a <strong>heading</strong> and <strong>small text</strong> on it.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/FYuiK4lq5A7pZbuU8ewO6w3CBboZBfi6gfqb.avif"],"a":"Lake of Constance","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Lake Constance</strong> (also known as <strong>Bodensee</strong>) lies on <strong>Austria’s western border</strong>. It's easy to recognize by its <strong>size</strong>, unmatched by other lakes in Austria’s <strong>mountain regions</strong>.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/GZqoUBQaMD9HHZt9qW6AZcm9CN8nm3MI29ky.avif"],"a":"Linz Street Signs","slug":"austria","note":"<p>In <strong>Linz</strong> you can find both <strong>blue signs</strong> with a <strong>unique font</strong> and <strong>white</strong> (red frame) with a <strong>coat of arms</strong> on them.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/KIUMdpoWyfOnGgEtXxpUV52wDqBHyRj5QpkR.avif"],"a":"Red White Pole Tape","slug":"austria","note":"<p>Poles in <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/@48.2081821,16.3325663,3a,75y,324.1h,77.26t/data=!3m7!1e1!3m5!1s_8i-ZITZMxduaUFv_-FJpQ!2e0!6shttps:%2F%2Fstreetviewpixels-pa.googleapis.com%2Fv1%2Fthumbnail%3Fcb_client%3Dmaps_sv.tactile%26w%3D900%26h%3D600%26pitch%3D12.74041282060007%26panoid%3D_8i-ZITZMxduaUFv_-FJpQ%26yaw%3D324.0996097884054!7i16384!8i8192?entry=ttu&#x26;g_ep=EgoyMDI1MDQyOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Vienna</a> and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/@47.2733985,11.4050673,3a,75y,271.27h,75.84t/data=!3m8!1e1!3m6!1sKCq73_JFBCjUGnXvN3tVmQ!2e0!5s20210101T000000!6shttps:%2F%2Fstreetviewpixels-pa.googleapis.com%2Fv1%2Fthumbnail%3Fcb_client%3Dmaps_sv.tactile%26w%3D900%26h%3D600%26pitch%3D14.162756602442187%26panoid%3DKCq73_JFBCjUGnXvN3tVmQ%26yaw%3D271.27024825309286!7i16384!8i8192?entry=ttu&#x26;g_ep=EgoyMDI1MDQyOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Innsbruck</a> often have <strong>red-and-white tape</strong> resembling the <strong>Austrian flag</strong>. In Vienna, the tape is <strong>thinner</strong>, usually with <strong>two strips</strong> per pole.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/k6FF7xfrgMbYyL2FwLB87EigsBnylGrlgwKJ.avif"],"a":"Salzburg Roadmarking","slug":"austria","note":"<p>A large <strong>white painted square</strong> in the middle of the road can be found next to kilometre markers in <strong>Salzburg</strong>.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/7sa7LFUnYCCqSskpYkVFGXDUlzEu9iX0BmNO.avif"],"a":"Styria Bus","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Styria</strong>´s public transport company is called \"<strong>RegioBus Steiermark</strong>\". The logo of it can be seen on busses in this region.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/aT3EDrwugmK3W9ijZfDtt570KcUv2A7OzjsN.avif"],"a":"Upper Austria Bus","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Upper Austria</strong>´s public transport company is called \"<strong>OÖVV</strong>\". The logo of it can be seen on busses in this region.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/087OKpn0ZNED2zB9jiV247ZH7Gl8sROt0Jhs.avif","https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/VhpTtihkSDtba4WYNHE6uq9pwRQH22NiWPxw.avif"],"a":"Vienna Bus","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Vienna</strong>´s public transport company is called \"<strong>Wiener Linien</strong>\". The logo of it can be seen on busses in/around the city. (<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/60f6054f4e76b03092956de8/201fed72-51ee-40bc-86d2-92e4dde9e3d4/Bus+companies.png?format=2500w\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">image</a>) <strong>NOTE:</strong> You can also see \"Wiener Linien\"/the logo on trams.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/R2U9vIj4hpp0J8TYNHRU2Vd2t0YbCWbs3Xik.avif"],"a":"Vienna Street Signs","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Vienna street signs</strong> are <strong>dark blue plaques</strong> with a classic white serif font. The number at the beginning shows the district you're in (see map).</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/VfcArJzkjorcShx4PepXmxnvc3BSkD2RuPvH.avif"],"a":"Vineyards","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Vineyards</strong> are limited to the far <strong>eastern part</strong> of the <strong>country</strong>.</p>\n<p>You can find a very precise map <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://vineyards.com/photos/maps/Austria%20Wine%20Map.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Notably, there are a lot of vineyards close to Vienna and around Lake Neusiedl.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/kS4Xi0B9QBpw14TXhVGpMzQDhUtkzQJaz5KK.avif"],"a":"Vorarlberg Bus Stops","slug":"austria","note":"<p>Bus stops consisting of <strong>neon-yellow poles</strong> are found in <strong>Vorarlberg</strong>.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/fevETurmTOCq1jGiWsh7bDj6EHyQfLMKW6Lz.avif"],"a":"Vorarlberg Kilometer Markers","slug":"austria","note":"<p>White <strong>kilometre markers</strong> can be found in <strong>Vorarlberg</strong> as well as on a road in <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://maps.app.goo.gl/xT2CxvJt4fdoTPXq5\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">western Salzburg</a>.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/oKqf3jJfJsFJExfJqNHpC7isJLnhKZVbhoqc.avif"],"a":"Vorarlberg Landbus","slug":"austria","note":"<p><strong>Vorarlberg</strong>´s public transport company is called \"<strong>Landbus</strong>\". The logo of it can be seen on busses in this region.</p>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/1271/cbIgPb86P46ZjjUGUBXv9B9DMTc5ZtMj7oyw.avif"],"a":"Vorarlberg Pole Markings","slug":"austria","note":"<p>These <strong>yellow</strong> and <strong>white stripes</strong> around <strong>poles</strong> and <strong>signposts</strong> are found in <strong>Vorarlberg</strong>.</p>"}]}